  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- During the clav solo Neal quotes Stevie Wonder's \"I Wish\", and the bass drum heard is Neal playing synth, not Alan [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Joyful Girl**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **Jesus Children**: back after 29 archived shows (450 days) [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Dig [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2003-5-17.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 11 songs; 125 min; rated 3/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says recording quality is very good, with Neal's bass keys coming through with real punch [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Alan stopped to repair something on his drum, so Neal filled the gap with a very long clavinet solo [1]\n- K'Alyn, from Me'Shell Ndegéocello's band, sang as a featured guest vocalist [1]\n- Reviewer notes the set mixes older and newer material nicely [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2003-5-17.shnf**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Michael Jurick; source: Neumann TLM 170s > Apogee AD1000 > DA-P1 > D8 [1]. Also: Reviewer says he patched and transferred the 5/16 show, but not this 5/17 one, so the listed source seems wrong [3]",
